  "subtitle": "The all-in-one digital phototypesetter where the operator reads a movable keyboard and a tiltable CRT, and watches remaining line length as a glowing light bar",
  "why_scout_cares": "A professional creative workstation whose HCI is genuinely novel: a movable keyboard, a 9-inch tiltable green-phosphor CRT, and an analog light-bar gauge on screen representing the remaining column space — a quasi-instrumented, non-textual measure of line length. Combined with foreground/background simultaneous editing and 14 programmable memory keys in 3 levels, this is an embodied, oddly-instrumented typesetting console with a verifiable primary-source brochure (Internet Archive) and NMAH archival holdings.",
